{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["Not because you are more numerous than all the peoples — men of understanding will wonder: was Moshe Rabbenu under the impression that Israel might be mistaken on this matter, thinking they were more numerous than all the nations in the world, so that he needed to say לא מרובכם?! And furthermore, since he said חשק ה׳ בכם — would HaShem love them because they are numerous?! Rather, this is its meaning: because he said above: ״ונשל גוים רבים מפניך החתי וגו׳״ — seven nations, numerous and mighty, more than you. Now perhaps you will say: we are more numerous than those seven peoples, and by our own might we will drive them out — לא מרובכם — you are not more numerous than all those seven peoples — ולא מרובכם חשק ה׳ בכם — to destroy them — כי אתם המעט — compared to all those peoples. כי — מאהבת ה׳ אתכם — because of His oath to your fathers, ונשל אותם מפניך."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The lemma is quoted as לא מרובכם (without the כי found in the verse). The word כי in the phrase כי מאהבת is rendered as 'because' rather than left as the deictic 'כי' since Rashbam appears to be reading it as causal."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:29.445574295Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}